course: dictionary
lesson: 13016
title: Extrude: squeezing out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To extrude something is to push or squeeze it out through a small opening. «Mia extruded the toothpaste from the tube onto her brush.» The clues are pushed and the small opening, so extrude means to squeeze something out.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Mia squeezed the toothpaste out through a small opening onto her brush.» If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: Factories and scientists use extrude in a special way. «The machine extrudes plastic pipes» means it forces plastic through a shaped hole, so it comes out as a long piece with that same shape.
fact: Extrude is a verb: extrude, extrudes, extruded, extruding.
fact: «Extrude» means to push or squeeze something out through a small opening.
fact: In industry, to extrude plastic, metal or pasta means forcing it through a shaped hole to make long pieces.
fact: «3D printers extrude melted plastic in thin lines.»
fact: «Volcanoes extrude lava onto the surface.»
exercise: «The machine extruded long pipes of plastic.» What does extruded mean? | *Pushed out through a shaped hole | Cut into tiny pieces | Melted and turned into water | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «The pasta machine extrudes dough through a star-shaped hole.» What is the dough doing? | Being painted | Being frozen solid | Being baked in an oven | *Being squeezed out through a hole
exercise: In 3D drawing software, extruding a flat shape turns it into what? | A sound | A flat drawing that gets smaller | *A 3D prism | A colour
test: «Lava was extruded from the volcano and cooled into rock.» What does extruded mean here? | Hidden deep under the ground | Blown up into the sky | Washed away by rain | *Pushed out onto the surface
test: Which of these is made by extrusion? | A sung song | A ball of wool | A painting | *A plastic pipe
exam: «Ella uses a 3D printer to extrude thin lines of melted plastic.» What is the printer doing? | *Pushing melted plastic out through a small opening | Drawing with a pencil | Cooling the plastic into ice | Mixing paint on a palette
